# SPPARKS additive/texture driven by the analytical
# Moser/Green's-function temperature source: a time-domain integral
# of an ellipsoidal Gaussian heat source against the unsteady heat
# kernel, on an insulating half-space (image source factor of 2).
#
# This is the same physics as the rosenthal_standard example
# (in.additive.rosenthal_standard) but expressed as the unsteady
# integral form of Moser et al. SAND2017 Eq. 4 instead of the
# steady-state Rosenthal closed-form. In the limit of constant
# parameters and a long enough emission history the two should
# agree to within the σ-vs-η reparameterization, modulo finite
# integration tolerance.
#
# Material:    rho ~= 8220 kg/m^3, cp ~= 650 J/(kg K), k = 11.2 W/(m K)
#              -> alpha = k/(rho*cp) = 2.0959e-6 m^2/s
# Laser:       Q=285 W (raw), lambda=0.155 (so absorbed = 44.2 W),
#              v=1.2 m/s
# Preheat:     T0=573 K, T_m=1573 K
#
# Note: the Moser source takes the *raw* laser power Q and absorption
# efficiency lambda separately, multiplying them internally to get the
# absorbed power. Compare to the Rosenthal example which folds the
# image-source factor of 2 into lambda (hence its lambda=0.0775).
# Here lambda=0.155 because the factor of 2 is now in the integrand
# prefactor of Eq. 4.
#
# Source widths sx, sy, sz are the std-devs of the ellipsoidal
# Gaussian deposition profile in the moving laser frame. With sx=sy
# the source is round in plan view; sz controls the depth of energy
# deposition. Values here are educated guesses for an LPBF spot of
# ~100 µm characteristic size; calibrate against a high-fidelity
# reference if you need quantitatively accurate pool dimensions.
#
# app_style args: nspins dx[m] dt[s] nrefine

app_style additive/texture 1000000 20e-6 5e-6 2

shell mkdir -p DumpFiles_moser

seed             56789

dimension        3
lattice          sc/26n 1.0
region           box block 0 60 0 40 0 20

boundary         n n n

create_box       box
create_sites     box
 set             site range 1 1000000
 set             i2 value 1
 set             d1 value 0
 set             d2 value 573

sector           yes
sweep            random mask no

diag_style       array d6 sum

temperature      0.0
misorientation_target gradient

liquidus         1573
solidus          1523
solid_front_vel  4 -1.0302e-7 1.0533e-4 2.2196e-3 0
nucleation_density      1e14
critical_undercooling   5
undercooling_deviation  3
mean_nuclei_volume      8.4375e-16
nuclei_volume_deviation 1.5625e-17

# ----- Moser Green's-function source ---------------------------------
# args: <Q[W]> <lambda> <k[W/(mK)]> <alpha[m^2/s]> <T0[K]> <cp[J/(kgK)]>
#       <sx[m]> <sy[m]> <sz[m]>
setup_temperature_source moser 285.0 0.155 11.2 2.0959e-6 573.0 650.0 50e-6 50e-6 25e-6

# Single linear scan, no repeats, exactly matching the rosenthal_standard
# example geometry. Coordinates in meters.
laser_path start 0.1e-3 0.4e-3 0.4e-3 end 1.1e-3 0.4e-3 speed 1.2 repeats 1

shell cd DumpFiles_moser

stats            1e-4

dump             1 text 2e-4 dump.moser.* id i1 i2 d6 x y z
dump_modify      1 thresh i2 > 1

# Run long enough to cover the full scan plus some cooling.
run              2e-3
shell cd ../
